<div class="panel demo">
  <b>Writing one word at a time vs refining all at once</b>
  <p class="caption">An autoregressive model writes one token per pass. A diffusion model starts with every position blank and fills in several per pass, most confident first.</p>
  <div class="small">Autoregressive</div><div class="dl" id="d-ar"></div>
  <div class="small">Diffusion</div><div class="dl" id="d-df"></div>
  <div class="row"><button class="btn pri" type="button" id="d-step">Step</button><button class="btn" type="button" id="d-play">Play</button><button class="btn" type="button" id="d-reset">Start over</button><span class="small" id="d-n"></span></div>
</div>
